C(453,[428],[136],'Hom_Pro(Y,X) ≃ Hom(limY,limX)','For target stages finitely presented over S and eventually affine systems, the comparison is an isomorphism when source stages are qcqs. The page explicitly adds qc only.','stated without proof',Q,'C','SearchC_Q06/C_Q19: Stacks01ZC Proposition32.6.1 gives the exact qcqs-source statement; EGAIV8.13.1 is the historical comparator. The proof uses quasi-separatedness to descend finitely many gluing equalities. We do not claim the broader qc-only text has been proved.',['C_Stacks01ZC','C_EGAIV2'],'high',present='As of November2026: established with qcqs source stages. The manuscript’s extra generality is not certified; its source conventions may contain an implicit restriction.')
C(454,[429],[138],'connu quand ... mod(t1,…,tn)^(N+1)','If m^(N+1)=0, evaluation of a formal series on m^n depends only on coefficients of total degree≤N.','stated without proof',O+'C01/C02; monomial filtration proof §6.','E','SearchC_Q11/C_Q12: standard nilpotent evaluation underlying formal smoothness and jets; Stacks00UP treats nilpotent lifting. The claim is directly proved by product degree and needs no assumption that nilpotent translations preserve the naive polynomial quotient.',['C_Stacks00UP'],'high')
C(455,[429],[138],'a_i∈m, det(bij)∉m','For a local ring with nilpotent maximal ideal, polynomials with constant terms in m and invertible linear coefficient matrix define a bijection m^n→m^n; successive differences are controlled by m^r/m^(r+1).','proof sketched',O+'C01/C02; induction in narrative §6.','E','SearchC_Q11/C_Q12: nilpotent inverse-function argument is standard in formal étale lifting, cf. Stacks00UP. Our induction solves corrections one filtration step at a time. The determinant must be a unit; the ambiguous scan138 symbols are not changed.',['C_Stacks00UP'],'high')
C(456,[429,430],[140],'Aut_Algèbre augmentée Z[t]/(t)^(N+1)','The augmentation-preserving automorphism functor of truncated n-variable polynomial algebras is represented by the coefficient scheme with invertible linear determinant; higher coefficients are unrestricted. It acts on m^n when m^(N+1)=0.','stated without proof',O+'C01/C03; filtered inverse proof §6.','B','SearchC_Q11/C_Q12: formal inverse-function and finite-jet constructions match the statement. Stacks00UP supplies the nilpotent lifting framework. Constants vanish in this augmentation-preserving group; arbitrary nilpotent translations are a distinct construction.',['C_Stacks00UP'],'high')
C(457,[431],[142],'espace affine sous T^0_(B0/A0)⊗V_i','A lift across a square-zero extension, when it exists, is a torsor under the appropriate module of derivations; the exact displayed T|J module is undeclared on the sheet.','stated without proof',Q,'C','SearchC_Q11/C_Q12: Stacks04FJ Lem37.9.5 gives the simply transitive Hom(a*Ω,J) action. The correspondence to the manuscript’s tensor expression needs smoothness/projectivity and identification of B0,A0 and V_i; it is conditional, not an exact transcription repair.',['C_Stacks04FJ'],'medium')
C(458,[430],[142],'a′0+a′1(a0+a1t+a2t²)+a′2(a0+a1t+a2t²)²','Quadratic substitution has coefficients c0=a′0+a′1a0+a′2a0², c1=a′1a1+2a′2a0a1, c2=a′1a2+a′2a1²+2a′2a0a2, with remainders2a′2a1a2t³+a′2a2²t⁴.','proved there',O+'C01 full exact expansion.','E','SearchC_Q11/C_Q12: elementary polynomial composition, independently recomputed. It supports the doubtful2 in the linear term. The literature on formal jets does not justify dropping higher terms unless the evaluation or quotient relation permits it.',['C_Stacks00UP'],'high')
C(459,[432],[142],'det(bij)≠0','If the displayed determinant condition is interpreted as merely nonzero over arbitrary rings, it does not define automorphisms.','false as stated',O+'C03: t↦2t over Z[t]/(t³) cannot be inverted.','F','SearchC_Q11/C_Q12: the correct open scheme is D(det), requiring the determinant to be a unit on ring-valued points, as in456. The source’s ≠0 can be conventional scheme-open notation, so this is a false literal interpretation, not a secure authorial error.',['C_Stacks00UP'],'high',present='As of November2026: false only under the literal nonzero-element interpretation; refined automorphism statement CL-SA03-456.')
C(460,[433],[142],'k[t]/(t³) beside a0+a1t+a2t²','Allowing arbitrary nilpotent constants does not define substitution automorphisms of A[t]/(t³).','false as stated',O+'C02: A=Q[ε]/ε³, (t+ε)³=3εt²+3ε²t≠0.','F','SearchC_Q11/C_Q12: augmentation-preserving jet automorphisms456 and nilpotent-set evaluation454 are distinct standard constructions. The sheet does not finish the identification; our counterexample targets only the naive quotient interpretation.',['C_Stacks00UP'],'high',present='As of November2026: the naive quotient reading is refuted; CL-SA03-454 is the valid nilpotent evaluation statement.')
C(461,[434],[119],'h∘g ... identité; g∘h ... identité','For a direct sum of modules, the exterior algebra is the graded tensor product of their exterior algebras, with the Koszul sign rule.','proved there',O+'C16; universal-property proof §7.','E','SearchC_Q13/C_Q18: Bourbaki AlgèbreIII §7 no7 is the published subject/section match, and Stacks00DM gives the exterior universal construction. The sheet is reused typescript, not evidence of a new authorial discovery. Exact internal typescript number371 is not dated.',['C_BourbakiAlgebra','C_Stacks00DM'],'high')
C(462,[434],[119],'Corollaire1 ... somme directe ... sum m_i=m','The degree-m exterior power decomposes as the direct sum over m1+…+mn=m of tensor products of the degree-mi exterior powers; the wedge expansion is the signed shuffle expansion.','proved there',O+'C16 determinants/shuffle; general multilinear argument §7.','E','SearchC_Q13/C_Q18: Bourbaki AlgèbreIII §7 no7 and Stacks00DM supply the established framework; the source’s explicit formula is checked by expanding multilinearly and sorting the factors by summand.',['C_BourbakiAlgebra','C_Stacks00DM'],'high')
C(463,[434],[123],'le diagramme ... est commutatif','The exterior-direct-sum isomorphism is natural in all summand module maps.','proved there',Q,'E','SearchC_Q13/C_Q18: this is the universal-construction naturality in Bourbaki AlgèbreIII §7. Our verification checks equality on degree-one generators, which generate both graded algebras. No Lefschetz-project conclusion follows.',['C_BourbakiAlgebra','C_Stacks00DM'],'high')
C(464,[434],[123],'Corollaire3 ... facteur direct','A split injection of modules induces a split injection of exterior algebras; the complementary summand is the graded ideal generated by a chosen complement.','proved there',Q,'E','SearchC_Q13/C_Q18: Bourbaki AlgèbreIII §7 no7 and exterior functoriality provide the standard result. The splitting hypothesis is retained; arbitrary injections of modules are not substituted.',['C_BourbakiAlgebra','C_Stacks00DM'],'high')
C(465,[434],[123,121],'Tout élément ... composante scalaire ... nulle ... nilpotent','Every element in the positive-degree ideal of the ordinary exterior algebra of any module is nilpotent.','proved there',O+'C17; finite-generator proof §7.','E','SearchC_Q13/C_Q18: the source proves this by restricting to finitely many generators. Stacks00DM supplies the exterior relations and filtered-colimit statement. This is elementwise nilpotence, not nilpotence of the full positive ideal when M has infinite rank.',['C_Stacks00DM','C_BourbakiAlgebra'],'high')
C(466,[434],[121],'Corollaire5 ... wedge(N∩P)=wedge(N)∩wedge(P)','If N∩P splits in both N and P and N+P splits in M, the embedded exterior subalgebras intersect in Λ(N∩P).','proved there',O+'C18; four-summand decomposition proof §7.','E','SearchC_Q13/C_Q18: this is the stated split direct-sum result in the reused text, consistent with Bourbaki AlgèbreIII §7. We do not drop the splitting hypotheses.',['C_BourbakiAlgebra','C_Stacks00DM'],'high')
C(467,[434],[121],'Proposition8 ... e_H ... une base','For a module with an ordered basis, wedges indexed by finite increasing subsets form a basis of its exterior algebra, including infinite-rank modules.','proved there',O+'C19; finite-subset colimit argument §7.','E','SearchC_Q13/C_Q18: Stacks00DM Lem10.13.1 and10.13.5 give free exterior powers and commuting filtered colimits; BourbakiIII§7 no8 is the exact standard section. The missing final continuation is replaced only by our separately labelled proof.',['C_Stacks00DM','C_BourbakiAlgebra'],'high')
C(468,[436],[127],'H^p(g,M)={0}; T=dρ+ρd','The exercise’s vanishing follows if its operator T is an invertible chain endomorphism homotopic to zero; the displayed representation-theoretic antecedents are not self-contained on this leaf.','proof sketched',O+'C22; h=T^−1ρ gives dh+hd=1.','F','SearchC_Q13/C_Q18: Bourbaki LieI exercises are a strong publication comparator, but missing definitions of h,β,T and prop12 prevent exact hypothesis recovery. We prove the sufficient chain lemma and do not assert general cohomology vanishing for every irreducible representation.',['C_BourbakiLie'],'medium')
C(469,[437],[129],'problème d’application universelle','The quotient U(g)/(x^p−x^[p]) is universal for restricted Lie homomorphisms from g into associative algebras in characteristic p.','stated without proof',Q,'E','SearchC_Q13/C_Q18/C_Q21: standard restricted enveloping algebra universal property; the reused exercise states it explicitly. Bourbaki LieI §2 exercise6 is the source locator; Ardizzoni2010/2012 gives a modern PBW comparator.',['C_BourbakiLie','C_Ardizzoni'],'high')
C(470,[437],[129],'0≤νλ<p ... une base','For a restricted Lie algebra free over its characteristic-p base ring, ordered monomials with exponents below p form a basis of the restricted enveloping algebra; g embeds.','proof sketched',O+'C21 counts only; triangular PBW proof §7.','E','SearchC_Q13/C_Q18/C_Q21: Bourbaki LieI §2 exercise6 gives the central x^p−x^[p] triangular proof. Ardizzoni’s Example4.6, preprint p12, recovers restricted PBW over a field; the broader free-ring version here is checked using ordinary PBW and a unit triangular change of basis.',['C_BourbakiLie','C_Ardizzoni'],'high')
C(471,[437],[129],'Toute dérivation intérieure est une p-dérivation','Inner derivations are restricted; every associative algebra derivation is restricted for its commutator p-Lie structure; for free g a derivation extends to the restricted enveloping algebra iff it is restricted.','proof sketched',O+'C20 and the ideal-preservation proof §7.','E','SearchC_Q13/C_Q18/C_Q21: Bourbaki LieI §2 exercise7 is the exact reused source. The computation uses (ad x)^(p−1)y=sum_j x^(p−1−j)yx^j modulo p, and preservation of x^p−x^[p] in the enveloping quotient.',['C_BourbakiLie','C_Ardizzoni'],'high')
C(472,[438],[139],'G n’est pas commutatif, mais ... Lie ... commutative','Over characteristic p>0 the displayed two-dimensional formal law is associative and noncommutative, while its Lie bracket vanishes.','stated without proof',O+'C06/C07, general Frobenius proof §7.','E','SearchC_Q13/C_Q18: the exact law appears in the indexed primary Bourbaki LieI §1 exercise27. Published book bibliographic link was opened; the mirrored PDF was searchable but its direct fetch failed. No independent historical priority is claimed from the undated reused draft.',['C_BourbakiLie'],'high')
C(473,[438,440],[141],'de degré total ≥3','The antisymmetric quadratic part of a formal group law gives the Lie bracket; a commutative formal group therefore has abelian Lie algebra.','proof sketched',O+'C06/C07/C12; coefficient derivation in §7.','E','SearchC_Q13/C_Q18: Bourbaki LieI §1 exercise24(c), retained in the supplied typescript; the exact quadratic formula was checked directly. Its converse fails by472 in positive characteristic.',['C_BourbakiLie'],'high')
C(474,[440],[141],'v→D(v∘F); (∂F_j/∂X_i)_c','A formal group homomorphism induces a Lie algebra homomorphism whose tangent matrix at the identity is the constant Jacobian, with the written row-index convention.','stated without proof',Q,'E','SearchC_Q13/C_Q18: Bourbaki LieI §1 exercise24(d) is the source. The target derivation must be defined at the identity and extended invariantly; the printed formula without that convention has codomain mismatch. We flag it rather than silently edit.',['C_BourbakiLie'],'medium')
C(475,[440],[141],'f_ij(u,v)=−δij+sum_k(δik+Uik)(δkj+Vkj)','The formal completion of GL_n at identity has dimension n² and law U+V+UV.','stated without proof',O+'C10 exact matrix expansion.','E','SearchC_Q13/C_Q18: Bourbaki LieI §1 exercise25 matches the printed law. The phrase group in n variables refers to the underlying representation degree, resolving the parallel symplectic wording.',['C_BourbakiLie'],'high')
C(476,[441],[143],'X_ij=(1+U_ii)D_ij+sum_(k≠i)U_kiD_kj','The displayed left-invariant GL_n derivations have matrix-unit brackets; in characteristic p, Xii^p=Xii and Xij^p=0 for i≠j.','stated without proof',O+'C11–C13; general generator proof §7.','E','SearchC_Q13/C_Q18: Bourbaki LieI §1 exercise25 continuation. We verify the left-translation differential and pth-iterate identities on generators, using that pth powers of derivations are derivations in characteristic p.',['C_BourbakiLie'],'high')
C(477,[439],[139],'XᵀA+AX=0','The symplectic tangent Lie algebra is the matrix subalgebra defined by XᵀJ+JX=0, of dimension n(2n+1), including characteristic2.','stated without proof',O+'C08/C09 plus block matrix proof §7.','E','SearchC_Q13/C_Q18: Bourbaki LieI §1 exercise26(c) gives the matrix equation. The word2n variables denotes representation degree, not a dimension claim. Symmetric off-diagonal blocks give the dimension in all characteristics.',['C_BourbakiLie'],'high')
C(478,[441],[139,143],'U=(I−R^−1S)^−1(I+R^−1S); S=R(U−I)(U+I)^−1','Over characteristic≠2 with invertible symmetric R, the two Cayley formulas are inverse on their determinant-open domains; they give the orthogonal formal chart and its multiplication. The tangent dimension is n(n−1)/2.','proof sketched',O+'C14/C15; general matrix identities §7.','E','SearchC_Q13/C_Q18: Bourbaki LieI §1 exercise26(a–b) is the exact supplied exercise; AlgèbreIX is referenced with blank sublocators. We verify the identities directly and do not invent the missing exercise number or off-leaf final assertion.',['C_BourbakiLie'],'high')

